# THE EMPTY-FRAME CASE, which is why both backends decide the type question from the
# SCHEMA rather than from the first value they see. There is no row here to learn
# from, and the column is still the wrong type — a backend reasoning from values
# would answer "fine, zero rows" while the other refused.
df = dataframe({n: [1, 2, 3]}).where(@n > 99)
print(df.count())
print(df.where(@n.starts_with("a")).count())
